padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"2\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">mustard seeds</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds a nutty flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"3\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">cumin seeds</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">enhances the aroma</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"4\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">fennel seeds (optional)</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds sweetness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"5\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">pinch</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">asafoetida (hing)</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">digestive aid</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"6\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2–3</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">pieces</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">dried red chilies</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for heat</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"7\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">8–10</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">leaves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">curry leaves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">fragrant herb</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"8\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1–2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">pieces</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">green chilies, slit</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds spice</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"9\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">small</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">onion, finely chopped</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">sweetness and depth</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"10\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cloves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garlic, thinly sliced</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">aromatic component</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"11\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">red chili powder (optional)</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">extra heat</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"12\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">enhances all flavors</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-7912-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"7912\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Small Pan&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For heating the oil and spices.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-7912-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-7912-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"7912\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation Steps</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7912-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: In a small pan, heat 2 tablespoons of oil or ghee over medium heat. Let it warm up nicely.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7912-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Add 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds and watch them splutter joyfully in the hot oil.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7912-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Next, toss in 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1 teaspoon of fennel seeds (if using), a pinch of asafoetida, and 2 dried red chilies. Sauté for a few seconds until fragrant.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7912-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Stir in a handful of curry leaves and 1-2 slit green chilies. Cook until they crisp up and release their aroma.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7912-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Add 1 chopped onion and a few slices of garlic. Sauté until they turn golden brown and delicious.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7912-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Sprinkle in some red chili powder (optional) and salt to taste. Stir well to combine all those lovely flavors.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7912-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 7: Finally, pour the hot tadka immediately over your dal, curry, or vegetables. Enjoy the burst of flavor!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-7912-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrition Facts</th>\n<th>Per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>100</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>9g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>2g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>5g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here&#8217;s everything you need to create the perfect <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dal#Tadka\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Indian tadka</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Indian-Tadka.webp\" alt=\"A vibrant arrangement of ingredients for Indian tadka on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-7910\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Indian-Tadka.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Indian-Tadka-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons oil or ghee</strong> – for tempering</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 teaspoon mustard seeds</strong> – adds a nutty flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 teaspoon cumin seeds</strong> – enhances the aroma</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 teaspoon fennel seeds (optional)</strong> – adds sweetness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 pinch asafoetida (hing)</strong> – digestive aid</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2–3 dried red chilies</strong> – for heat</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>8–10 curry leaves</strong> – fragrant herb</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1–2 green chilies, slit</strong> – adds spice</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 small onion, finely chopped</strong> – sweetness and depth</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 garlic cloves, thinly sliced</strong> – aromatic component</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 teaspoon red chili powder (optional)</strong> – extra heat</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Salt to taste</strong> – enhances all flavors</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-indian-tadka\"><strong>How to Make Indian Tadka</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to elevate your dishes with this delightful Indian tadka! With a preparation time of just 5 minutes and a cooking time of 10 minutes, you’ll have a flavorful tempering ready to enhance your meals. No extra resting time is needed, so let’s dive right in!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Exploring-the-Creation-of-Indian-Tadka.webp\" alt=\"A visual depiction illustrating the various phases involved in preparing Indian Tadka, showcasing the array of spices and cooking techniques.\" class=\"wp-image-7920\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Exploring-the-Creation-of-Indian-Tadka.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Exploring-the-Creation-of-Indian-Tadka-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Heat the Oil or Ghee</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a small pan, heat 2 tablespoons of oil or ghee over medium heat. Let it warm up nicely.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Add Mustard Seeds</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add 1 teaspoon of mustard seeds and watch them splutter joyfully in the hot oil.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Sauté the Spices</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Next, toss in 1 teaspoon of cumin seeds, 1 teaspoon of fennel seeds (if using), a pinch of asafoetida, and 2 dried red chilies. Sauté for a few seconds until fragrant.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Add Curry Leaves and Green Chilies</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Stir in a handful of curry leaves and 1-2 slit green chilies. Cook until they crisp up and release their aroma.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Sauté Onions and Garlic</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add 1 chopped onion and a few slices of garlic. Sauté until they turn golden brown and delicious.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Season the Tadka</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sprinkle in some red chili powder (optional) and salt to taste. Stir well to combine all those lovely flavors.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Pour Over Your Dish</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Finally, pour the hot tadka immediately over your dal, curry, or vegetables. Enjoy the burst of flavor!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Condiment / dinner</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Indian</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>5 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Over dal, curry, or vegetables</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-indian-tadka\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Indian Tadka</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Always use fresh spices for the best flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat the oil until it&#8217;s shimmering for a perfect tempering.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add spices in the right order to maximize their aroma.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with different lentils for unique tastes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Finish with a squeeze of lemon for a zesty kick.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-indian-tadka\"><strong>How to Serve this indian tadka</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Drizzle over steamed basmati rice for a fragrant kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix into lentil dishes like dal for extra flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use as a topping for roasted vegetables to elevate their taste.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with warm naan or chapati for a delightful meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add to soups for a spicy, aromatic finish.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside yogurt or raita to balance the heat.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and enjoying your Indian tadka later is easy and convenient:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow the tadka to cool completely.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transfer to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label the container with the date for easy tracking.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool the tadka completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use freezer-safe containers or bags.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Leave some space for expansion when sealing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for up to 2 months for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight if frozen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat on the stovetop over low heat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of water or oil to maintain moisture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Stir occasionally until heated through.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What is Indian tadka?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Indian tadka, also known as tempering, is a cooking technique used in Indian cuisine where spices are briefly cooked in hot oil or ghee to release their essential oils and flavors. This aromatic mixture is then added to dishes like dals, curries, and vegetables to enhance their taste and aroma.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What ingredients are typically used in Indian tadka?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Common ingredients for Indian tadka include mustard seeds, cumin seeds, dried red chilies, curry leaves, and garlic. You can also use ginger, asafoetida (hing), and green chilies for added flavor. The choice of spices can vary based on regional preferences and the dish being prepared.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. How do you prepare a basic Indian tadka?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To prepare a basic Indian tadka, heat oil or ghee in a pan over medium heat. Once hot, add mustard seeds and let them splutter. Then, add cumin seeds, dried red chilies, and curry leaves. Sauté for a few seconds until fragrant, and if desired, add minced garlic or ginger. Finally, pour this tempering over your prepared dish for a burst of flavor.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Which dishes commonly use Indian tadka?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Indian tadka is commonly used in various dishes, including lentil soups (dal), vegetable curries, and rice dishes. It adds a rich flavor and aroma, making it a staple in many Indian households. You can also use it to enhance the taste of simple dishes like sautéed greens or even salads.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now that you have the authentic Indian tadka recipe in your hands, it’s time to bring some warmth and flavor to your kitchen! This simple yet rewarding dish is perfect for elevating your meals. So gather your spices, unleash your inner chef, and enjoy the delightful aroma and taste of homemade tadka. Happy cooking!</p>\n",
